{"itemKind": "mcq", "contentVersion": "pres-simple-001", "knowledgePointRef": "grammar.present_simple", "skillRef": "grammar", "payload": {"sentence": "I ___ to school by bus.", "choices": ["go", "am go", "going", "am going to"], "answer": "go", "explanation": "「行きます」は go だけで表します。日本語の「です・ます」につられて am を足さないことが大切です。"}}
{"itemKind": "mcq", "contentVersion": "pres-simple-002", "knowledgePointRef": "grammar.present_simple", "skillRef": "grammar", "payload": {"sentence": "We ___ English every day.", "choices": ["study", "are study", "studying", "are studied"], "answer": "study", "explanation": "一般動詞の文に be動詞は入れません。be動詞と一般動詞は同時に使えないと覚えます。"}}
{"itemKind": "mcq", "contentVersion": "pres-simple-003", "knowledgePointRef": "grammar.present_simple", "skillRef": "grammar", "payload": {"sentence": "They ___ soccer after school.", "choices": ["play", "are play", "plays", "playing"], "answer": "play", "explanation": "they は複数なので s は付けません。"}}
{"itemKind": "mcq", "contentVersion": "pres-simple-004", "knowledgePointRef": "grammar.present_simple", "skillRef": "grammar", "payload": {"sentence": "I ___ breakfast at seven every morning.", "choices": ["have", "am have", "has", "having"], "answer": "have", "explanation": "「朝ごはんを食べる」は have で表せます。主語が I なので has にはしません。"}}
{"itemKind": "mcq", "contentVersion": "pres-simple-005", "knowledgePointRef": "grammar.present_simple", "skillRef": "grammar", "payload": {"sentence": "My friends ___ in Tokyo.", "choices": ["live", "lives", "are live", "living"], "answer": "live", "explanation": "friends は複数なので s は付きません。"}}
{"itemKind": "mcq", "contentVersion": "pres-simple-006", "knowledgePointRef": "grammar.present_simple", "skillRef": "grammar", "payload": {"sentence": "We ___ TV after dinner.", "choices": ["watch", "see", "look", "are watch"], "answer": "watch", "explanation": "テレビは watch です。see は「目に入る」、look は「目を向ける」で、意識して見続けるのは watch です。"}}
{"itemKind": "mcq", "contentVersion": "pres-simple-007", "knowledgePointRef": "grammar.present_simple", "skillRef": "grammar", "payload": {"sentence": "I ___ music every night.", "choices": ["listen to", "listen", "hear", "am listen"], "answer": "listen to", "explanation": "「音楽を聞く」は listen to です。to を落とすとつながりません。"}}
{"itemKind": "mcq", "contentVersion": "pres-simple-008", "knowledgePointRef": "grammar.present_simple", "skillRef": "grammar", "payload": {"sentence": "You ___ very fast.", "choices": ["run", "runs", "are run", "running"], "answer": "run", "explanation": "you が主語のときは s を付けません。"}}
{"itemKind": "word_order", "contentVersion": "pres-simple-009", "knowledgePointRef": "grammar.present_simple", "skillRef": "grammar", "payload": {"japanese": "わたしは毎日英語を勉強します。", "blocks": ["I", "study", "English", "every", "day"], "answers": [["I", "study", "English", "every", "day"]], "explanation": "英語は「だれが→する→何を→いつ」の順です。日本語の「毎日」が先に来るのとは違います。"}}
{"itemKind": "word_order", "contentVersion": "pres-simple-010", "knowledgePointRef": "grammar.present_simple", "skillRef": "grammar", "payload": {"japanese": "彼らは放課後サッカーをします。", "blocks": ["They", "play", "soccer", "after", "school"], "answers": [["They", "play", "soccer", "after", "school"]], "explanation": "「放課後」は文の最後に置きます。"}}
{"itemKind": "word_order", "contentVersion": "pres-simple-011", "knowledgePointRef": "grammar.present_simple", "skillRef": "grammar", "payload": {"japanese": "わたしたちはバスで学校へ行きます。", "blocks": ["We", "go", "to", "school", "by", "bus"], "answers": [["We", "go", "to", "school", "by", "bus"]], "explanation": "手段を表す「〜で」は by です。go to school の to を落としやすいので注意します。"}}
{"itemKind": "word_order", "contentVersion": "pres-simple-012", "knowledgePointRef": "grammar.present_simple", "skillRef": "grammar", "payload": {"japanese": "わたしは毎朝７時に起きます。", "blocks": ["I", "get", "up", "at", "seven", "every", "morning"], "answers": [["I", "get", "up", "at", "seven", "every", "morning"]], "explanation": "時刻には at を使います。get up は 2 語で「起きる」です。"}}
